  ],
  "equipment_type": "Pump (CIF-Module BACnet interface)",
  "applies_to": "Wilo Yonos GIGA2.0-I / -D glandless inline pumps fitted with a CIF-Module BACnet MS/TP or Ethernet Multiprotocol (BACnet IP).",
  "summary": "The Yonos GIGA2.0 takes the same CIF-Modules as the Stratos GIGA2.0 for BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP, with a smaller object set (no energy metering or reference temperatures). The BMS writes on/off, control mode and a relative duty point, and keeps control alive with a bus command timer. It reports speed, power, head, calculated flow and energy, plus warning and error codes, and exposes override, preset (fallback) and auxiliary parameter sets.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "CIF-Module 1.00-6.01 (EDE); datapoint list valid to 6.11",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Object list taken from Wilo's EDE file for this pump (CIF-Module BACnet MS/TP and Ethernet Multiprotocol files list the same objects); names follow Wilo's datapoint list.",
    "Objects ending Prs are preset (startup / bus-failure fallback) values; objects ending Aux belong to the auxiliary parameter set chosen with MO 34.",
    "A few objects (e.g. AI 50, AI 51) need CIF-Module firmware 5.01 or later. Wilo's Ethernet Multiprotocol EDE shortens a few names (e.g. busCmd.TimerAct for MO 1, controlFunctionPrsLim for MO 100); names here follow the MS/TP EDE and the datapoint list.",
    "Multistate state lists show the values Wilo marks as supported for this pump; error-code objects use Wilo's E-code numbering (value = code + 1)."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Write the control mode (MO 0), the duty point setpoint in % (AO 0) and the on/off command (BO 0). To keep BMS control safe, write SET to the bus command timer (MO 1) more often than its timeout (AO 8, default 300 s); use SET_PRESET if the pump should load the Prs fallback values when the BMS goes quiet. Read status from BI 10, BI 13 and MI 1.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 0",
        "name": "device/functionOnInp",
        "why": "Pump on/off command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 0",
        "name": "controlFunctionInp",
        "why": "Control mode, e.g. dp-c, dp-v, constant speed"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 0",
        "name": "dutyPointRelInp",
        "why": "Duty point setpoint, % of the control range"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 1",
        "name": "busCmd.TimerInp,Act",
        "why": "Heartbeat: write SET (2) before the timeout"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 10",
        "name": "device/functionOnOut",
        "why": "Pump on"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 15",
        "name": "localOperationOut",
        "why": "Local override; BMS not in control"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "speedP01Out",
        "why": "Pump speed, rpm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "powerInputOut",
        "why": "Electrical input power, W"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 13",
        "name": "errorPresentOut",
        "why": "Any active error"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 1",
        "name": "warning/errorMessageOut",
        "why": "Wilo error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Once the CIF-Module is set up, the pump's setpoint, control mode and on/off follow the values held in the module, not the local menu. BI 15 shows when a local action is overriding BMS control. MO 3 selects where the setpoint comes from (1 = IF-Module).",
    "heartbeat": "MO 1 bus command timer: write SET (2) again before the timeout in AO 8 (default 300 s). If it runs out the local menu is released and the display may show E50/E54; with SET_PRESET (6) the pump also loads the preset (Prs) on/off, control mode and duty point. Writing MANUAL (5) unlocks the local menu permanently; OFF (1) returns to the factory behaviour.",
    "remote_sensors": "AO 11 accepts an external sensor value from the BMS; the selected value reads back on AI 2011.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP: the bus address set in the pump menu is the MS/TP MAC; 0-127 = manager (default use), 128-254 = subordinate.",
      "Baud rate is set with parameter A in the pump menu (9600 to 115200, plus 76800).",
      "The device instance is entered in the pump menu as parameters C, E and F; how the number is split across them depends on the pump type (Wilo's datapoint list has a calculator).",
      "CIF-Module Ethernet: extended settings via a web browser on port 80; default hostname is wilo- plus the ETH1 MAC address."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AO 0 is a relative duty point; its range is not always 0-100 % and 0 % does not mean off. AI 33 gives the value that equals 100 %, with its units in MI 33.",
      "The flow reading (AI 2) is calculated and should not be used for closed-loop control.",
      "Commandable objects use priority 16 as a floating default; relinquishing every priority returns the static relinquish default (BO 0 = off, AO 0 = 100 %).",
      "BI 18 actuationLimitOut means the speed output is at a limit, so the pump cannot follow further changes in that direction."
    ]
  },
